-- title:
--   Cohomological triviality of the splitting module in Tate's theorem
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite group, let $C$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-linear representation of $G$, and let $\varphi$ be a $2$-cocycle of $C$ (an element of `groupCohomology.cocycles₂ C`), with cohomology class `groupCohomology.H2π C φ`. Assume: (i) for every subgroup $S \le G$ the degree-$1$ group cohomology of the restriction of $C$ along the inclusion $S \hookrightarrow G$ is a zero object; (ii) for every finite subgroup $S \le G$ one has $\#H^2(S, C) = \#S$; and (iii) for every subgroup $S \le G$ the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of the single element obtained by applying the restriction map in degree $2$ induced by $S \hookrightarrow G$ (with the identity on the restricted coefficients) to the class of $\varphi$ is all of $H^2(S,C)$. Then for every finite subgroup $S \le G$ and every $q \in \mathbb{Z}$, the degree-$q$ Tate cohomology of the restriction to $S$ of the splitting module [`Rep.splittingModule C φ`](def/GroupCohomology_SplittingModule.html#L124) is a zero object. Here the splitting module is $C \times I_G$, with $I_G = \ker(\varepsilon) \subset \mathbb{Z}[G]$ the augmentation ideal, carrying the action $\sigma\cdot(v,x) = (\rho_C(\sigma)v + \mathrm{cocycleTwist}(C,\varphi)(\sigma)(x),\ \sigma x)$, the twisting term being built from $\varphi$; and Tate cohomology means ordinary group cohomology in degrees $\ge 1$, group homology in degrees $\le -2$ (degree $-n-2$ giving $H_{n+1}$), the invariants modulo the image of the norm map in degree $0$, and the kernel of the norm map in degree $-1$.
--
--   This is the cohomological triviality statement at the heart of Tate's theorem: under the hypotheses that $H^1(S,C)$ vanishes and $H^2(S,C)$ is cyclic of order $\#S$ generated by the restriction of a fixed class, the module splitting that class has vanishing Tate cohomology over all subgroups. It is used by [`Rep.IsTateCupProduct.bijective_cup_of_h1_h2`](thm.html#Rep.IsTateCupProduct.bijective_cup_of_h1_h2) to obtain the cup-product isomorphism in Tate's theorem with coefficients.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Rep_isZero_tateCohomology_res_splittingModule.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GroupCohomology_TateCohomology
import Definitions.Def_GroupCohomology_SplittingModule

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false
universe u
open CategoryTheory Rep

theorem Rep.isZero_tateCohomology_res_splittingModule {G : Type} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (C : Rep ℤ G) (φ : groupCohomology.cocycles₂ C)
    (h1 : ∀ (S : Subgroup G), CategoryTheory.Limits.IsZero (groupCohomology (Rep.res S.subtype C) 1))
    (h2card : ∀ (S : Subgroup G) [Fintype S], Nat.card (groupCohomology (Rep.res S.subtype C) 2) = Fintype.card S)
    (h2gen : ∀ (S : Subgroup G),
      Submodule.span ℤ {(groupCohomology.map S.subtype (𝟙 (Rep.res S.subtype C)) 2).hom (groupCohomology.H2π C φ)} = ⊤)
    (S : Subgroup G) [Fintype S] (q : ℤ) :
    CategoryTheory.Limits.IsZero ((Rep.res S.subtype (Rep.splittingModule C φ)).tateCohomology q) := by sorry
